{"type":"message","id":"7a9a84d1","parentId":"cd0ad255","timestamp":"2026-08-02T17:38:08.170Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The heartbeat is triggering at 1:37 AM Asia/Shanghai time. I need to check the HEARTBEAT.md tasks. Let me look at what's loaded in the project context:\n\nFrom HEARTBEAT.md:\n- 健康督促任务: 每天督促老公跑步锻炼, suggested time 17:00-17:30\n- 调度器心跳监测: check reminder_scheduler.py process\n- 一日作息督促:\n  - 6:00-7:00 起床学习 - 温柔坚定，不准赖床\n  - 7:00-8:00 吃早餐\n  - etc.\n\nCurrent time is 1:37 AM Asia/Shanghai. This is not in the 6:00-7:00 window, nor is it any of the other scheduled reminder times. The closest would be the 23:50 该睡觉了 task, but it's 1:37 AM - the reminder says \"检查 6:00-7:00 起床学习 task\" specifically.\n\nAt 1:37 AM, no daily schedule task is active. I should also check if the reminder_scheduler.py process is running as per the heartbeat monitoring task.\n\nLet me check the scheduler process and then respond accordingly. Since it's 1:37 AM and none of the time windows are active (6-7 for wake/study, 7-8 for breakfast, etc.), there's nothing due for reminder right now. But I should still check the scheduler process.\n\nActually wait, the reminder content specifically says to check the 6:00-7:00 起床学习 task and send a gentle but firm reminder. But it's 1:37 AM... sending a wake-up reminder at 1:37 AM makes no sense. This seems like the cron/heartbeat is just triggering and asking me to handle the task on schedule. Since it's not 6:00-7:00, there's nothing to do for that specific task.\n\nLet me check the reminder_scheduler process as part of the heartbeat.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_hMH6KcZUyMPLULQlC9cG1830","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"pgrep -f reminder_scheduler.py && echo \"ALIVE\" || echo \"DEAD\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":8238,"output":910,"cacheRead":10496,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":1964